    dynamic_runtime_lane_dual_rt_definitions_2026-09-06, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep6: the lane is Windows-host-unreachable by construction (stage4 gate), so reproduced at the exact link-composition level with tree-built ingredients: a fixture linked shared-runtime + full supplement showed 851 dual-defined names across exe + .so (829 rt_* + 22 spl_*; current-tree analogue of the doc's 509), silent at runtime exactly as documented. Root cause: the dynamic lane appended the FULL core-C supplement after the shared runtime (linker.rs:2374 old; build_core_c_runtime_supplement_library builds the unprojected archive). Fix: tools.rs project_dynamic_runtime_core_c_supplement + dynamic_runtime_supplement_gap_symbols (3 unit tests) - projects the supplement via the existing oracle-gated project_stage4_archive_closure: strong-retain only single-defined archive globals the runtime does NOT export; runtime-owned passengers weakened to owner-overridable fallbacks; gap set prefix-blind (preserves lazy-extraction semantics). linker.rs read_shared_runtime_export_set reads the real export set (ELF dynsym / Mach-O trie / PE exports; nm -g deliberately avoided - 165 names are present-but-not-exported). Verification: AFTER on real artifacts - 1027 duals removed, 0 residual strong duals, 0 multi-defined gap roots lost; cargo check clean; 3/3 unit tests; lane check-stage4-dynamic-runtime-lane PASS 3/3 with the patched seed; runtime_bundle_duplicate_sources 12/12; no regression on native_link_hardening (identical outcome set patched vs unpatched). Residuals: end-to-end fixed-lane run needs Linux/macOS (gap logic unit-tested + verified against the real artifact pair); check-rt-dual-implementation-ratchet has no dynamic-lane coverage - a Linux-side nm gate would pin duals at 0. close_evidence reproducer=src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/tools.rs prevention=src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/native_project/linker.rs"

